# Installed beside detir-shell and waid-runtime (config/packages.chroot).
# Their dependencies pull in labwc, chromium, gnome-keyring, fonts and Mesa.
# Install Cerlus alongside the shared WAID runtime; it remains a separate product.
cerlus
sudo
# Wired and Wi-Fi connections (nmcli, nmtui); nothing else configures the network.
network-manager
# ifconfig, netstat and route: Debian 13 no longer installs them by default, and people reach for them.
net-tools
# arecord, aplay, alsamixer and amixer, for checking sound and microphone hardware.
alsa-utils
# Scripts the installer's language list shows (Indic, Thai, Japanese, Korean, Chinese);
# without them those names draw as boxes. detir-shell's `fonts-noto-core | fonts-dejavu-core`
# is met by DejaVu alone, so the Noto fonts are named here.
fonts-noto-core
fonts-noto-cjk
# The Terminal draws a fixed-width font and looks it up by name; DejaVu Sans Mono is one the
# text engine knows. Without it the Terminal falls back to a proportional font and its prompt,
# cursor and typed text drift apart. The Noto fonts above are not enough.
fonts-dejavu-core
# Remote login to an installed system, for development and support. It does not run on live
# media (see etc/systemd/system/ssh.service.d), where the login password is public.
openssh-server
